// MUST FAIL: a struct declared with enum syntax — brace-less, comma-separated
// members. Structs are brace-delimited (DESIGN.md:345, 119, 536); enums are not
// (DESIGN.md:392, 1027). PLAN.md:139 calls that asymmetry "the asymmetry to get
// right". A brace-less body may contain variants, never `name: T` fields.

Point* =
    x: f64,
    y: f64
